IVI message book - EReg
=======================

resources/compiled/fields.php holds the names, units and code values of the fields of the Initial
Vehicle Information (IVI) from the IVI message book, version 1.11 of 2025-04-02, published
by Topic Group XII of the Association of European Vehicle and Driver Registration Authorities (EReg).
The names of the fields of IVI 2.0 in resources/layout/certificate.php follow the draft of its XML
schema of 2025-02-27, the codes of IVI 2.0 in resources/translations/codes-*.php this draft as well.

Sources: resources/messagebook/SOURCE.md.


Regulations of the European Union
=================================

The labels of the numbered items (resources/translations/items-*.php), the words of the tables of
point 49 (resources/translations/render-*.php) and the types of bodywork
(resources/translations/codes-*.php) are the official German, English and French wording of Annex VIII
of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2020/683 and of Annex I of Regulation (EU) 2018/858, as
published on EUR-Lex. Their reuse is authorised, see
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/content/legal-notice/legal-notice.html. Only the texts in the Official
Journal of the European Union are authentic.

Sources: resources/messagebook/SOURCE.md.


Own translations
================

Where no official wording exists, the texts in resources/translations are the package's own (MIT, like
the rest of the package): the headings and hints of the document, the names of the columns of the table
of NEDC values, the meaning of many codes in German and French, the titles of the rare fields
(resources/translations/fields-en.php).


Dependencies
============

Not part of this package: Composer installs them as separate packages, each under its own license.
The PDF output (Render\PdfRenderer) uses dompdf/dompdf (LGPL-2.1) with dompdf/php-font-lib
(LGPL-2.1-or-later), dompdf/php-svg-lib (LGPL-3.0-or-later), masterminds/html5 (MIT) and
sabberworm/php-css-parser (MIT), and the font DejaVu Sans that comes with dompdf. The booklet
(Render\Booklet) uses setasign/fpdi and setasign/fpdf (MIT).
